PART 3: Operators 
 
Types of Operators 
 
Arithmetic: Used with numeric values to perform common mathematical operations.  
+ (Addition) 
 - (Subtraction) 
 * (Multiplication) 
/ (Division: yields a float) 
// (Floor Division: rounds down to nearest whole number) 
% (Modulus: returns division remainder) 
** (Exponentiation: raises a number to a power) 
 
Assignment: Used to assign values to variables. 
= (Simple assignment: x = 5) 
+= (Add and assign: x += 3 is x = x + 3) 
-= (Subtract and assign) 
*= (Multiply and assign) 
/= (Divide and assign) 
 
Comparison: Compares two values and returns a boolean result (True or False). 
== (Equal to) 
!= (Not equal to) 
> (Greater than) 
< (Less than) 
>= (Greater than or equal to) 
<= (Less than or equal to) 
 
